# Phase-6 momentum-phase probe: reach phase 2 cheaply.
#
# The open Phase-6 item "momentum-phase asymptotics" was blocked because no run in
# the dynamic-verification set reached phase 2 — the default
# `transition_trigger = cooling_balance` keeps simple_cluster in the implicit phase
# for the whole affordable window.
#
# `transition_trigger blowout` is a documented, schema-registered alternative
# (registry.py:408): it drives the energy->momentum transition on R2 > rCloud
# instead. The phase6_short run logs
#   "R1 shadow: BLOWOUT (R2>rCloud) would fire at t=9.083857e-02 Myr, R2=1.729 pc"
# so this config reaches the transition at t ~ 0.09 Myr rather than never, which
# buys enough momentum-phase snapshots to fit R(t).
#
# Physics is otherwise identical to harness/phase6_short.param
# (mCloud 1e5 Msun, sfe 0.3, homogeneous, rCloud = 1.6900 pc).
#
# NOTE: this changes WHICH criterion ends the energy phase, so it is not a
# trajectory-equivalent replica of phase6_short — it is a config chosen to make
# phase 2 reachable, and any exponent measured here describes THIS run.
mCloud    1e5
sfe    0.3
stop_t    0.5
transition_trigger    blowout
